  "notes": "Source table on page 64 provides retirement rates by Age (rows) and Years of Service (columns). Target requires Service (rows) x Age (columns), so transpose=true. Source rates are in percent; values_unit='percent' ensures conversion to decimal. Source service bins are 'Under 30' ([null, 29]) and '30 or More' ([30, null]). Target service bins map via overlap_weighted: '5-11' through '25-29' fall entirely within 'Under 30', so they copy that rate. '30' through '40' fall entirely within '30 or More', so they copy that rate. Target age columns 50-69 map directly to source rows. Target age '70' (70+) maps to source row '70' via copy. Although the source has rows for 71-75+, the target grid defines '70' as '70 and over'. Since the source rates for 70, 71, 72, 73, 74, and 75+ are identical (22.0/25.0/50.0/50.0 depending on service), copying the '70' row value is mathematically equivalent to the weighted average of the 70+ block. Using 'copy' avoids the 'share_even' constraint violation for multiple sources.",
